{"info": {"author": null, "author_email": "Herv\u00e9 BREDIN <herve@pyannote.ai>", "bugtrack_url": null, "classifiers": [], "description": "![pyannote.core](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pyannote/pyannote-core/main/.github/social-preview.png)\n\n> advanced data structures for handling and visualizing temporal segments with attached labels.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\n$ pip install pyannote.core\n```\n\nSupport for graphical visualization in Jupyter notebooks can be added with:\n\n```bash\n$ pip install pyannote.core[notebook]\n```\n\n## Documentation\n\nThe documentation is available at [http://pyannote.github.io/pyannote-core](http://pyannote.github.io/pyannote-core).\n\nSample notebooks are available [here](https://nbviewer.jupyter.org/github/pyannote/pyannote-core/blob/develop/notebook/index.ipynb).\n\n## Citation\n\nIf you use `pyannote.core` in your research, please use the following citation:\n\n```bibtex\n@inproceedings{pyannote.metrics,\n author = {Herv\\'e Bredin},\n title = {{pyannote.metrics: a toolkit for reproducible evaluation, diagnostic, and error analysis of speaker diarization systems}},\n booktitle = {{Interspeech 2017, 18th Annual Conference of the International Speech Communication Association}},\n year = {2017},\n month = {August},\n address = {Stockholm, Sweden},\n url = {http://pyannote.github.io/pyannote-metrics},\n}\n```\n", "description_content_type": "text/markdown", "docs_url": "https://pythonhosted.org/pyannote-core/", "download_url": null, "downloads": {"last_day": -1, "last_month": -1, "last_week": -1}, "dynamic": null, "home_page": null, "keywords": null, "license": null, "license_expression": null, "license_files": ["LICENSE"], "maintainer": null, "maintainer_email": null, "name": "pyannote-core", "package_url": "https://pypi.org/project/pyannote-core/", "platform": null, "project_url": "https://pypi.org/project/pyannote-core/", "project_urls": null, "provides_extra": ["doc", "notebook", "test"], "release_url": "https://pypi.